the repo set up! =F0=9F=8E=89 Getting the file in is the easy part =E2=80=
=94 here's the dead-simple way (no Git commands, all through the browser), =
then how to flip on the live link.</p>
<h2>=F0=9F=93=A4 Step 1 =E2=80=94 Upload the file</h2>
<ol>
<li>Go to your <strong>Rando</strong> repo page on github.com (you'll be lo=
oking at it now =E2=80=94 probably says <em>"quick setup"</em> or shows a m=
ostly empty repo).</li>
<li>Click <strong>Add file</strong> (top right, near the green Code button)=
 =E2=86=92 <strong>Upload files</strong>.</li>
<li>Drag your <strong><code>Rant-o-Meter.html</code></strong> file into the=
 box (or click <em>"choose your files"</em> and pick it).</li>
<li>Scroll down to <strong>Commit changes</strong> and click the green <str=
ong>Commit changes</strong> button. That's it =E2=80=94 the file's in. =E2=
=9C=85</li>
</ol>
<h2>=F0=9F=8C=90 Step 2 =E2=80=94 Turn on GitHub Pages (this makes it click=
able)</h2>
<ol>
<li>In your repo, click <strong>Settings</strong> (top menu of the repo).</=
li>
<li>Down the <strong>left sidebar</strong>, click <strong>Pages</strong>.</=
li>
<li>Under <strong>"Build and deployment"</strong> =E2=86=92 <strong>Source<=
/strong>, choose <strong>Deploy from a branch</strong>.</li>
<li>Under <strong>Branch</strong>, pick <strong>main</strong> (or <em>maste=
r</em>), leave the folder as <strong>/ (root)</strong>, and click <strong>S=
ave</strong>.</li>
<li>Wait about <strong>1=E2=80=932 minutes</strong>, then refresh that page=
. A green banner appears with your live link.</li>
</ol>
<h2>=F0=9F=94=97 Step 3 =E2=80=94 Your shareable link</h2>
<p>Your URL will look like this:</p>
<pre node=3D"[object Object]"><code>https://YOUR-USERNAME.github.io/Rando/R=
ant-o-Meter.html
</code></pre>
<p>Just swap in your actual GitHub username. Send <em>that</em> link to any=
one =E2=80=94 they click it and the meter loads live in their browser, butt=
ons and all. =F0=9F=96=B1=EF=B8=8F=F0=9F=94=A5</p>
<h2>=E2=9A=A1 Pro tip</h2>
<p>If you rename the file to <strong><code>index.html</code></strong> inste=
ad of <code>Rant-o-Meter.html</code>, the link gets shorter and cleaner:</p=
>
<pre node=3D"[object Object]"><code>https://YOUR-USERNAME.github.io/Rando/
</code></pre>
<p>Both work =E2=80=94 <code>index.html</code> just looks tidier when you s=
hare it.</p>
